  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures a Mountain Goats performance from Thursday, February 20, 2003, at Herrgårn in Linköping, Sweden [1]. The setlist features eleven songs, including \"Linda Blair Was Born Innocent,\" \"Neon Orange Glimmer Song,\" and \"Cheshire County\" [1]. Notable tracks include \"All Devils Here Now,\" which is the first in the archive and considered a mythic rarity with only two archived performances, and \"I Wonder Where our Love Has Gone,\" a rare cut with five archived performances [1]. The show also includes \"Tallahassee,\" \"Your Belgian Things,\" \"The Monkey Song,\" \"Southwood Plantation Road,\" \"Some Swedish Trees,\" and \"The Sign\" [1]. This is the 40th show in the archive's collection for the band, following a previous archived show on February 18, 2003, at Uffes Kallare [2]. The recording was captured using AT933 cardioid microphones connected to a battery box and a Sharp MD-SR70 minidisc recorder [1]. Taped by whilethisbox, the audio file contains the full eleven-song set with a total duration of forty minutes [1]. As the only available recording of this specific date, it offers a complete look at the band's setlist for this leg of their tour [1].",
